{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCenteringOfQ3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCenteringOfQ3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.inv_cube_bar_invariant_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.inv_cube_bar_invariant_iff","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L247-L262","doc":"**`q⁻³` is bar-invariant only in the degenerate case.**  So no reading of it\nas a state-attached factor escapes the asymmetry except at `q⁶ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.fbor_mirror_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.fbor_mirror_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L237-L245","doc":"**The whole bar-asymmetry of `F_Bor` is `q⁶`, and it comes only from `/q³`.**\n\nBoth ingredients are bar-blind, so the mirror ratio is exactly the square of the\napplied normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.fBor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.fBor","kind":"def","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L234-L235","doc":"`F_Bor` as the code computes it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.trM_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.trM_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L224-L232","doc":"**`tr_M(β_Bor)` is bar-invariant**: the closed form is even in `h`, and\n`h ↦ −h` under `q ↦ q⁻¹`. So the trace does not distinguish a state from its\nconjugate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.trMBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.trMBorromean","kind":"def","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L218-L222","doc":"The Lean-proved Borromean Markov trace as a function of `q`, via\n`h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.no_writhe_prefactor_yields_inv_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.no_writhe_prefactor_yields_inv_cube","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L164-L180","doc":"**Attempt 2: no writhe prefactor can produce `q⁻³` on this braid.**\n\n`markov-axioms-primitive.md` states that link invariance is restored by the\n*writhe prefactor outside the trace*. Such a prefactor is a function of the\nwrithe alone and multiplicative in it — `w ↦ a^w`. On `β_Bor` the writhe is `0`,\nso **every** such prefactor equals `1`, whatever `a` is. Hence none yields the\n`q⁻³` that `F_Bor` applies, unless `q³ = 1` — and at the substrate `q₀ ≈ 1.11`\nit is not.\n\nThis is the sharp form of the negative: `/q³` does not merely lack a derivation\ntrail, it is **unreachable** by the normalisation rule the corpus itself states,\nevaluated on the corpus's own braid word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.writhe_prefactor_is_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.writhe_prefactor_is_one","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L159-L162","doc":"**Every writhe prefactor is trivial on `β_Bor`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.borromean_writhe_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.borromean_writhe_zero","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L156-L157","doc":"**`β_Bor` has writhe zero** — three negative and three positive crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.borromeanWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.borromeanWord","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L152-L154","doc":"`β_Bor = (σ₁⁻¹σ₂)³`, the braid word the corpus assigns to the Borromean\nrings (`borromean-markov-trace-closed-form.md:2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.writhe","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L148-L150","doc":"A braid word as a list of signed generators; only the **sign** of each entry\nmatters for the writhe (`+i` is `σᵢ`, `−i` is `σᵢ⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.code_form_eq_poincare_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.code_form_eq_poincare_bar","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L134-L146","doc":"**Attempt 1, sharpest form: the code's factor is the BAR-CONJUGATE of the\nPoincaré polynomial.**\n\n`[3]_q!^bal / q³ = P(q⁻¹)`. `P` is palindromic, so one centering reaches the\nsymmetric point and the second overshoots it by the same amount, landing on `P`\nevaluated at the inverse variable. This is exactly what \"double centering\"\nmeans. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.ell_w0_eq_n_iff_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.ell_w0_eq_n_iff_three","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L110-L128","doc":"**`n = 3` is the degenerate strand count.**\n\n`ℓ(w₀) = n(n−1)/2` coincides with `n` exactly at `n = 3`, so a single 3-strand\ninstance cannot separate \"center by `ℓ(w₀)`\" from \"one power per strand\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.balanced_is_bar_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.balanced_is_bar_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L102-L108","doc":"**The once-centered form is bar-symmetric**: `[3]_q!^bal` is invariant under\n`q ↦ q⁻¹`. This is the symmetry the second division destroys. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.code_form_is_doubly_centered","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.code_form_is_doubly_centered","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L93-L100","doc":"**The code's object is centered twice.**\n\n`F_Bor` divides the balanced factorial by `q³` again, landing at\n`P(q) / q⁶ = q^{−2ℓ(w₀)} · P(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.balanced_is_already_centered","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.balanced_is_already_centered","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L84-L91","doc":"**The balanced factorial is already the centered Poincaré polynomial.**\n\n`[3]_q!^bal = P(q) / q³` — one factor of `q^{ℓ(w₀)}`, `ℓ(w₀) = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.qFactThreeBalanced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.qFactThreeBalanced","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L80-L82","doc":"The balanced `[3]_q!`, written from the balanced integers\n`[2] = q + q⁻¹` and `[3] = q² + 1 + q⁻²` (the `[1]` factor is `1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.poincareS3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PoincareCentering.poincareS3","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PoincareCenteringOfQ3.lean#L76-L78","doc":"The Poincaré polynomial of `S₃` in the variable `q²`:\n`P(q) = Σ_{w ∈ S₃} q^{2ℓ(w)} = 1 + 2q² + 2q⁴ + q⁶`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}